# An example of what `satellite_admin.py acl` produces. The real file is generated from
# the node registry; this one is here to be read, not installed.
#
# The shape is the whole point: a node writes only under its own name and reads only its
# own commands. There is no topic a satellite can publish to that another satellite reads,
# so a node that is taken over cannot speak for the house.

user sentry-mode-hub
topic read sentry/v1/nodes/+/events
topic read sentry/v1/nodes/+/state
topic read sentry/v1/nodes/+/health
topic read sentry/v1/nodes/+/acks
topic write sentry/v1/nodes/+/commands
topic write sentry/v1/nodes/+/state

user zero-entrance
topic write sentry/v1/nodes/zero-entrance/events
topic write sentry/v1/nodes/zero-entrance/state
topic write sentry/v1/nodes/zero-entrance/health
topic write sentry/v1/nodes/zero-entrance/acks
topic read sentry/v1/nodes/zero-entrance/commands
